schema: '0.4'
id: cola_js-02-dense-stress-layout
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: cola_js
category: network-and-graph-visualization
variant: dense-graph-stress-layout
prompt:
  context:
  - references/fim/overview/network-3d-graphics/cola_js.md
  - references/fim/solution/cola_js.md
  text: 'Build a WebCola stress-layout demo for a dense incident dependency graph with

    about 600 nodes, 1800 links, and 25 grouped subsystems. Precompute or warm the

    layout before first paint, use symmetricDiffLinkLengths or jaccardLinkLengths,

    avoidOverlaps(true), handleDisconnected(true), and staged start iterations.

    Render with D3 SVG for a filtered subset and include a performance panel that

    reports node count, edge count, constraints, layout phase, elapsed milliseconds,

    and unresolved overlaps. Include an explicit fallback note that very large live

    constraint solves should be precomputed or moved to a worker.

    '
  system: You generate artifacts for cola_js. Output only the requested artifact content. No markdown fences, no explanations.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 6144
    temperature: 0.3
output:
  formats:
  - format: html
  - format: json
  renderer: d3-svg
  expected_artifact: Stress test page plus serialized layout diagnostics.
  text_format: cola_js
  artifact_kind: Stress test page plus serialized layout diagnostics.
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - Uses WebCola as a layout engine with realistic iteration controls.
  - Includes dense graph stress metrics and a filtered rendering strategy.
  - Explains precompute or worker fallback for heavy constraint solving.
  - Avoids promising smooth live interaction for unbounded graph sizes.
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    description: YAML parses and declares formats, renderer, and diagnostics.
    criteria: YAML parses and declares formats, renderer, and diagnostics.
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    description: Covers dense graph, constraints, overlap avoidance, and performance reporting.
    criteria: Covers dense graph, constraints, overlap avoidance, and performance reporting.
  - name: Visual/structural quality
    weight: 25
    description: Stress view remains legible through filtering, grouping, and diagnostic overlays.
    criteria: Stress view remains legible through filtering, grouping, and diagnostic overlays.
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    description: Includes safeguards for convergence limits, overlap checks, and large graph fallback.
    criteria: Includes safeguards for convergence limits, overlap checks, and large graph fallback.
  pass_conditions:
  - The prompt respects WebCola performance limits and layout-only role.
  - The dense scenario includes measurable stress indicators.
  - The rendered subset and JSON diagnostics can be evaluated independently.
tags:
- fim
- cola-js
- webcola
- dense-graph
- stress-layout
- constraints
- diagnostics
